    {
      "title": "OpenAPI 3.1 Mental Model and Document Structure",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "OpenAPI 3.1 Mental Model and Document Structure",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What OpenAPI Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==contract==: language-neutral, machine-readable, YAML or JSON",
                "Describes an **HTTP API**; one file feeds Swagger UI, codegen, mocks, linters",
                "**OpenAPI** = the spec; **Swagger** = tooling around it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Document Structure",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`openapi`",
                  "spec version string, e.g. `3.1.0` {red:(required)}"
                ],
                [
                  "`info`",
                  "`title` + `version` {red:(required)}"
                ],
                [
                  "`servers`",
                  "base URLs"
                ],
                [
                  "`paths`",
                  "endpoints and operations"
                ],
                [
                  "`components`",
                  "reusable parts"
                ],
                [
                  "`security`",
                  "default auth"
                ],
                [
                  "`tags`",
                  "operation grouping"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "openapi: 3.1.0",
                "info:",
                "  title: Pets API",
                "  version: 2.4.0",
                "paths: {}"
              ],
              "note": "minimal valid document"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Two versions",
              "text": "`openapi` is the spec version; `info.version` is your API's own. They are ==unrelated==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. What 3.1 Changed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Schemas align with ==JSON Schema 2020-12==",
                "New top-level `webhooks` map: provider-initiated calls",
                "Need at least one of `paths`, `components`, `webhooks`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**OpenAPI vs Swagger?** Spec vs tooling; Swagger was the spec's old name",
                "**Required top-level?** `openapi`, `info`, plus one of paths, components, webhooks",
                "**3.1 vs 3.0?** JSON Schema 2020-12 alignment and `webhooks`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Paths, Operations and Parameters",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Paths, Operations and Parameters",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Path items and operations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`/users/{id}` is a ==path item==: one operation per HTTP method",
                "Methods: `get`, `post`, `put`, `patch`, `delete`",
                "Each operation has a ==unique operationId==",
                "Codegen uses `operationId` as the **method name**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Parameters",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "`in`",
                "Carried in",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`path`",
                  "URL template",
                  "`/users/{id}`"
                ],
                [
                  "`query`",
                  "after `?`",
                  "`?limit=10`"
                ],
                [
                  "`header`",
                  "HTTP header",
                  "`X-Request-Id`"
                ],
                [
                  "`cookie`",
                  "Cookie header",
                  "`session`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Path parameters need ==required: true==",
                "The `name` must match the `{name}` in the URL template"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Request body and responses",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`requestBody.content` is keyed by **media type**, with a `schema`",
                "`responses` are keyed by ==status code==, plus optional `default` for errors"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "operationId: createUser",
                "requestBody:",
                "  content:",
                "    application/json:",
                "      schema: {$ref: '#/components/schemas/NewUser'}",
                "responses:",
                "  '201': {description: Created}",
                "  '422': {description: Validation error}"
              ],
              "note": "a post operation"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "3.1 responses rule",
              "text": "`responses` is ==optional== in 3.1 (3.0 required it). If present, list at least one status code. Document errors too: **400, 401, 404, 422**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Schemas, Components and $ref Reuse",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Schemas, Components and $ref Reuse",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Components and $ref",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`components` holds ==schemas==, parameters, responses, requestBodies, securitySchemes, examples",
                "Define once, reuse everywhere with `$ref`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "components:",
                "  schemas:",
                "    User:",
                "      properties:",
                "        nick: {type: [string, 'null']}",
                "# usage",
                "schema:",
                "  $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'"
              ],
              "note": "$ref points at a JSON Pointer"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. 3.1 vs 3.0",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "3.0",
                "3.1"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Nullable",
                  "`nullable: true`",
                  "`type: ['string','null']`"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "`example`",
                  "`examples` (array)"
                ],
                [
                  "exclusiveMinimum",
                  "boolean",
                  "{green:number}"
                ],
                [
                  "$ref siblings",
                  "ignored",
                  "`description`, `summary` ok"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Composition",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Keyword",
                "Matches",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`allOf`",
                  "all",
                  "merge / extend"
                ],
                [
                  "`oneOf`",
                  "exactly one",
                  "alternatives"
                ],
                [
                  "`anyOf`",
                  "one or more",
                  "flexible union"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`discriminator.propertyName` names the field that picks the subtype",
                "Tools use it to deserialize polymorphic payloads"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why $ref?** One definition, no drift",
                "**Nullable?** 3.1 type array; 3.0 `nullable`",
                "**oneOf vs allOf?** Choose one vs combine; discriminator selects"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Design-First vs Code-First, Clients and Contract Testing",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Design-First vs Code-First, Clients and Contract Testing",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Design-First vs Code-First",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Design-first",
                "Code-first"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Order",
                  "Spec, then code",
                  "Code, then spec"
                ],
                [
                  "Spec from",
                  "Consumer review, then stubs and mocks",
                  "Annotations: FastAPI, springdoc"
                ],
                [
                  "Docs match",
                  "By discipline and CI",
                  "==By construction=="
                ],
                [
                  "Pick for",
                  "Public or multi-team APIs",
                  "Fast internal, single team"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Generate Clients",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "openapi-generator-cli generate -i openapi.yaml -g typescript-axios -o ./client"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`openapi-typescript` for ==types only==",
                "Regenerate in ==CI==",
                "{red:Never hand-edit} generated output"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Contract Testing",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Checks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Schemathesis==",
                  "Fuzzes the live API against the spec"
                ],
                [
                  "Dredd, Prism",
                  "Validate requests and responses against spec"
                ],
                [
                  "==Pact==",
                  "Consumer-driven: what consumers use"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "schemathesis run openapi.yaml --url http://localhost:8000"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Beyond unit tests",
              "text": "Contract tests catch ==drift== between spec and live responses: wrong status, missing field, bad type."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Design vs code-first?** Contract first for public APIs; code-first for one team's service.",
                "**Client?** Generate in CI from the spec; version it with `info.version`.",
                "**Contract tests catch?** Spec and behaviour drift that mocked unit tests miss."
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Keeping Docs in Sync and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Keeping Docs in Sync and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lint and Diff in CI",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Spectral== ruleset: naming, required descriptions, `operationId` rules",
                "`redocly lint` also validates the spec",
                "==Breaking change== = removed field, new required param, narrowed enum",
                "Diff against the main branch; a breaking change {red:fails the build}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "spectral lint openapi.yaml",
                "redocly lint openapi.yaml",
                "oasdiff breaking --fail-on ERR old.yaml new.yaml"
              ],
              "note": "run on every PR; old.yaml comes from main"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Single Source of Truth",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Source",
                "Generates",
                "CI guard"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Spec",
                  "Code, stubs, clients",
                  "Regenerate; never hand-edit output"
                ],
                [
                  "Code",
                  "Spec file",
                  "Fail if committed spec is stale"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Drift",
              "text": "A hand-edited spec beside hand-written code ==drifts==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing error responses (400, 401, 404, 422)",
                "Undeclared `required`: properties are ==optional== unless listed",
                "Duplicate `operationId` values",
                "Loose schema: no `additionalProperties` decision",
                "`example` that does not match its schema"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Stop drift?** One source of truth; CI regenerates and fails on a stale spec",
                "**Breaking change?** Removed field, new required param, narrowed enum",
                "**CI wiring?** `spectral lint`, `redocly lint`, then `oasdiff breaking` vs main"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
